"""Root adjudication of the eleven differing blind crops on scan058."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,json
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];p='151_scan058';r=json.loads((W/'reports'/f'{p}.json').read_text());t=(W/'pages'/f'{p}.tex').read_text();dec={}
def d(b,decision,changed,evidence):dec[b]={'decision':decision,'changed':changed,'evidence':evidence}
d('b02','retain first','no','Both readings give the same rounded scripted letters, separate bars and dot, set-difference stroke, minus, intersection, and ij indices in (5). Only math wrappers, spacing commands and grouping braces differ; no terminal punctuation is visible.')
d('b03','retain first','no','The whole (6) crop confirms the contracted script V, intersection, both i indices, raised star and detached final point. Bracing and display wrappers do not change this reading.')
d('b04','qualify cancelled index; retain live formula','yes','The whole three-row formula and the tight detail were viewed. The blackened old index has a tall curved body and surviving lower curl: add ell as an alternative to i. The wavy stroke is wholly below k and ends before the less-than sign; it is an underline of k, not a lesssim relation. Above the second-row live bar the separate horizontal mark has cancellation teeth but no secure original function; retain the unsure old dash. All live letters, bars, dots, indices, relations and final point agree with the first reading.')
d('b05','qualify cancelled index; retain other first readings','yes','The surviving lower loop and long curved blackened upper body admit ell as well as i. Retain i as the first proposal and add ell. The short wavy underline is directly under k, not under the less-than sign. The separate old horizontal mark is crossed by short upward teeth; an unsure dash remains a more informative cautious reading than an unidentified character.')
d('b06','retain first','no','The first subscript is ii with no comma, the later ones i,i with separate commas. The round bowls and looped right return support script V. The long last-chain underline runs to the sheet edge. The blind differences are grouping and math-mode syntax only.')
d('b07','retain first','no','Both readers give pierres. Its two consecutive r shoulders are clear after the looped e. Each quote is a pair of short raised straight strokes; TeX opening and closing quote syntax encodes the same marks as the blind straight quotation marks.')
d('b08','retain first','no','Both readings preserve the comma between i and j in the starred term and its absence in the unstarred term, plus the separate comma between terms. The script letters have closed upper loops and round bowls; only bracing and math delimiters differ.')
d('b09','accept blind word after ink review','yes','The initial low open e-like body has a small angular accent above it; the next body is a single shallow v followed by a detached i stroke before the tall looped d. There are not separately recoverable n and c bodies. The tall t and final es agree. On this enlarged word and its whole-line context, évidentes is the better reading; the first-pass confident incidentes is withdrawn. Confidence is medium because the opening is compressed.')
d('b10','retain first diagram','no','The whole diagram has three arrows with the same directions, quoted âme and right-side comma. The left letter combines a round bowl/right cap with full crossing diagonals; no secure pen order establishes which component is cancelled. Retain the live V/X alternative without inventing a cancelled layer. The tiny tick before 9 is visible, but gives no secure prime-label function; retain the documented pen-contact interpretation. The neighbouring word is decided in b09 and the inserted les belongs to the following line.')
d('b11','retain first unresolved object','no','Both crossing diagonals and the rounded lower bowl with projecting upper-right cap survive. Their overlap does not establish a readable deletion/replacement sequence. Retain the script-V/X uncertainty. The downward arrow is already included in the full diagram, not a new character in this object.')
d('b12','retain first','no','The opening ces has a low c, consistent with the preceding comma; there is no enlarged capital. Both readers have pierres, with separate r shoulders. After compr- the low nearly horizontal ending does not distinguish a from e securely, so retain comprenant/comprennent. The raised les has its own long curved insertion leader; the upper X_j star and downward arrow belong to the diagram above and are already transcribed there.')
old=r'\deleted{\unsure{i}}';new=r'\deleted{\unsure{i|\ell}}'
assert old in t and 'inclusions incidentes' in t
t=t.replace(old,new).replace('inclusions incidentes','inclusions évidentes')
for q in r['changes']:
 if q['id']=='r11':q.update(final=new,evidence=dec['b05']['evidence'])
 if q['id']=='r30':q.update(final='évidentes',evidence=dec['b09']['evidence'],confidence='medium',diff_c=False,diff_h=True)
for q in r['decisions']:
 if q['id']=='M1004':q.update(decision='first',reading='évidentes',evidence=dec['b09']['evidence'],confidence='medium')
for q in r['doubts']:
 if q['place']=='(7), old union-index glyph':q.update(reading=new,alternatives='i / ell / unidentified old glyph',reason=dec['b05']['evidence'])
r['notes'].append('scan058.N11. Blind adjudication changes incidentes to évidentes: the low initial e-like body, small raised angular accent, single shallow v and separate i before d support the blind reading, at medium confidence. The earlier high-confidence contrary evidence in the first-pass snapshot is superseded. The old union index now admits i/ell. The wave is under k alone, not a lesssim sign. No pen-order claim is made for the overlaid diagram letter; no prime is assigned to the small contact tick before 9. The low final verb still leaves comprenant/comprennent unresolved. Both occurrences of pierres have independently visible paired r shoulders.')
with (W/'second'/f'{p}_comparison.tsv').open() as f:comp={q['box']:q for q in csv.DictReader(f,delimiter='\t')}
with (W/'second'/f'{p}_boxes.tsv').open() as f:boxes={q['box']:[int(q[k]) for k in ('x0','y0','x1','y1')] for q in csv.DictReader(f,delimiter='\t')}
finals={b:comp[b]['first'].replace(old,new) for b in ['b04','b05']};finals['b09']='évidentes'
r['second_changes']=[{'box_id':b,'place':'blind box '+b,'first':comp[b]['first'],'second':comp[b]['second'],'final':v,'evidence':dec[b]['evidence'],'crop':f'crops/second_{p}_{b}.jpg','box':boxes[b],'confidence':'medium' if b=='b09' else 'low'} for b,v in finals.items()]
(W/'pages'/f'{p}.tex').write_text(t);(W/'reports'/f'{p}.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');(W/'audit'/f'{p}_adjudication.json').write_text(json.dumps(dec,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
